R2 (additive energy) vs |R|/(6/7)^k at critical V=floor(7s/6). AP=max R2, Sidon=min R2.
R2(AP_13)=k(k-1)(2k-1)/3=1300. (6/7)^13=0.13480.
          family     R2 longAP  |R|/lead
         AP-full   1300     13    0.6108
        7-struct    420      4    0.0338
             mid    316      4    0.0524
      low-energy    288      3    0.1008
       Sidon-ish    216      3    0.0510

=> if |R|/lead rises monotonically with R2 and stays <1 for dissociated (low R2),
   the a-priori |R|<(6/7)^k reduces to an R2 (additive-energy) threshold -- THM-660 territory.
